# Kiesel: the telegraph pebbles that trickle down a Steinschlag column
# before a rock drops (renderer only, no collision). Two grey grains: a 2x2
# grain i/m and a single i grain, each with a k underside so they read on
# pale limestone and on dark rock alike. fall: the grains swap height.
sprite = kiesel
size   = 4x4
origin = 2,4
hitbox = 0,0,4,4
anim   = fall frames=2 ticks=4 loop
---
frame fall 0
im..
mk..
...i
...k
frame fall 1
...i
...k
im..
mk..
